{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015u37JZtYUN1dUjPkYMYMhi","type":"tool_result","content":"61:         * @description Stellar: returns an unsigned XDR to sign and submit via /v2/tx/submit. SOLANA: for an external (SIWS) wallet only, returns the unsigned transaction custody compiled, to sign with the wallet and submit via /v2/tx/submit with the same idempotencyKey. Platform-managed wallets on other chains: /v2/tx/build-sign-submit.\n132:         * @description Stellar: a signed XDR. SOLANA: the transaction /v2/tx/build returned, signed by the external wallet, with the build's idempotencyKey; custody adds the sponsor signature when the token is sponsored.\n152:         * @description Platform-managed wallets. `chain` defaults to STELLAR, which behaves exactly as v1. SOLANA takes an SPL/SOL transfer and POLYGON a POL/ERC-20 transfer, both with integer base-unit amounts and a required idempotencyKey. An external Solana wallet uses /v2/tx/build and /v2/tx/submit instead.\n267:         * @description Deprecated. Use POST /v2/tx/build-sign-submit, which is multichain and records the tx.\n16058:declare function createApiClient(baseUrl: string, options?: ApiClientOptions): openapi_fetch.Client<paths, `${string}/${string}`>;\n16536:    baseUrl?: string;\n16967:    /** API origin + version prefix (e.g. `https://sdk.api.pollar.xyz/v3`). */\n----\n    /** Every route between the fiat and the asset, quoted leg by leg, best first. */\n    quoteRamp(body: RampQuoteRequest): Promise<RampQuotesResponse>;\n    /**\n     * Turns a quote the user accepted into an order. `payee` holds a value for each\n     * of the quote's `requiredFields` (`rampQuoteFields`); a missing or wrong one is\n     * refused before anything moves. The same quote always answers the same order.\n     */\n    createRampOrder(body: RampOrderRequest): Promise<RampOrder>;\n    getRampOrder(id: string): Promise<RampOrder>;\n    /** Asks about the order's fiat payment now, for a