{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RH6ntzX7P4GGkBHzF4eCgj","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-sNafh7/package.json has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bce8851-e926-4120-9d22-c63185adba0d","uuid":"c04a7414-380e-4a14-ba10-2cd2cc7c2fe5","timestamp":"2026-11-09T22:27:54.999Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-sNafh7/package.json","oldString":"  \"scripts\": {\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\"\n  },","newString":"  \"scripts\": { \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\" },","originalFile":"{\n  \"name\": \"tipjar\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@pollar/core\": \"^0.12.0\",\n    \"@pollar/react\": \"^0.12.0\",\n    \"react\": \"^18.3.1\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"^18.3.1\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/react\": \"^18.3.12\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"^18.3.1\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.6.3\"\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":9,"newStart":2,"newLines":7,"lines":["   \"name\": \"tipjar\",","   \"private\": true,","   \"type\": \"module\",","-  \"scripts\": {","-    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\"","-  },","+  \"scripts\": { \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\" },","   \"dependencies\": {","     \"@pollar/core\": \"^0.12.0\",","     \"@pollar/react\": \"^0.12.0\","]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RH6ntzX7P4GGkBHzF4eCgj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt9DEqkoWYqgHsgC9cDc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SqHM9EeDHMY6EPEyuvEjCg","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-sNafh7/ANSWER.md","content":"# Pollar 0.10 → 0.12 upgrade\n\nThe app now uses `@pollar/core` and `@pollar/react` `^0.12.0`, the current `latest` on npm. `npx tsc --noEmit` passes.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- `package.json`: `@pollar/core` and `@pollar/react` moved from `^0.10.1` to `^0.12.0`.\n- `package-lock.json` regenerated by `npm install`.\n\n## Changes by file\n\n### `src/pollar.ts`: API endpoint (the retirement fix)\n- `baseUrl` was `https://sdk.api.pollar.xyz/v1`. In 0.12, `baseUrl` is an origin only, and the SDK appends its own `/v3` prefix. The `/v1` path is the one being retired on 2026-11-30, so it is now `https://sdk.api.pollar.xyz`.\n\n### `src/trust.ts`: \"Accept USDC\"\n- `setTrustline(USDC, { sponsored: true })` became `setTrustline(USDC)`. 0.12 removed the `sponsored` option. Sponsorship is now on by default: the app covers the 0.5 XLM reserve and fee when eligible, which is what the old flag asked for. Only the `skipSponsorship` opt-out remains.\n\n### `src/ramp.ts`: \"Add money\" rate\n- `getRampsQuote({ country, currency, amount, direction })` no longer exists. The replacement is a two-step flow: `getRampRoutes('ONRAMP')` lists the fiat and asset pairs, then `quoteRamp(...)` quotes one.\n- The new code finds every route for ARS in AR to USDC, quotes each one for `10_000` ARS (`denomination: 'in'`), and returns the lowest pesos-per-USDC rate. The old code took the first quote's `rate`, which 0.12 no longer returns, so the rate is now computed as `amountIn / amountOut`.\n- Routes or quotes that find no path (`SDK_RAMPS_NO_ROUTE`) are treated as \"no quote\", so the function still returns `null` when nothing quotes. Other errors are rethrown.\n- The `Wallet` screen is unchanged: it still shows `1 USDC = {rate} ARS`.\n\n### `src/balances.ts`: wallet balances\n- `WalletBalanceRecord.balance` is now `string | null`. `null` means the chain could not be read. The old code called `parseFloat` on it, which would throw a type error (and a `NaN` at runtime). A `null` balance now renders as `\"<CODE> unavailable\"`, not as zero, as the SDK asks.\n\n### `src/kyc.ts`: KYC status message\n- `KycStatus` gained `'expired'`. The `switch` now handles it with the line \"Verification expired\". The `switch` had no default, so without this case the typecheck fails.\n\n### `src/App.tsx`, `src/Wallet.tsx`\n- No change. `PollarProvider`, `usePollar`, `login`, `wallet`, `walletBalance`, `refreshWalletBalance` and `getClient` all still exist with the same shapes in 0.12.\n\n## Assumptions to check\n\n- **Ramp units.** The 0.12 typings do not say whether `amountIn` and `amountOut` are human-readable decimals or base units. I assumed decimals, as in the request's `amount.value`. If they are base units, the rate is off by a fixed factor.\n- **Ramp rails.** The app previously let the server choose the payment rail. The new code quotes all AR/ARS/USDC routes, so it is the same request, expressed per rail.\n- **Trustline return value.** `enableUsdc` still returns `true` only for `status === 'success'`. 0.12 can also return `'pending'` (the server-orchestrated path, where the hash is optional). That still returns `false`, as before. I did not change it.\n- **Not tested against the network.** I did not call the Pollar API. The app uses a demo testnet key, and the typecheck is the only check I ran.\n\n## Not done\n\n- No deploy, publish or external submission.\n- `node_modules/` is not in `.gitignore` and appears as untracked. I did not commit it or change `.gitignore`.\n- The 0.12 README points to an `UPGRADE.md` at the repo root that is not in the published package. I used the package's typings and README instead.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3138,"cache_read_input_tokens":79230,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3138},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bce8851-e926-4120-9d22-c63185adba0d","uuid":"ade17998-b8ee-46c9-a270-3640b17381da","timestamp":"2026-11-09T22:28:01.217Z","request_id":"req_011Cgt9DEf67Brdacp8nn8b8","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SqHM9EeDHMY6EPEyuvEjCg":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-sNafh7/ANSWER.md","content":"# Pollar 0.10 → 0.12 upgrade\n\nThe app now uses `@pollar/core` and `@pollar/react` `^0.12.0`, the current `latest` on npm. `npx tsc --noEmit` passes.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- `package.json`: `@pollar/core` and `@pollar/react` moved from `^0.10.1` to `^0.12.0`.\n- `package-lock.json` regenerated by `npm install`.\n\n## Changes by file\n\n### `src/pollar.ts`: API endpoint (the retirement fix)\n- `baseUrl` was `https://sdk.api.pollar.xyz/v1`. In 0.12, `baseUrl` is an origin only, and the SDK appends its own `/v3` prefix. The `/v1` path is the one being retired on 2026-11-30, so it is now `https://sdk.api.pollar.xyz`.\n\n### `src/trust.ts`: \"Accept USDC\"\n- `setTrustline(USDC, { sponsored: true })` became `setTrustline(USDC)`. 0.12 removed the `sponsored` option. Sponsorship is now on by default: the app covers the 0.5 XLM reserve and fee when eligible, which is what the old flag asked for. Only the `skipSponsorship` opt-out remains.\n\n### `src/ramp.ts`: \"Add money\" rate\n- `getRampsQuote({ country, currency, amount, direction })` no longer exists. The replacement is a two-step flow: `getRampRoutes('ONRAMP')` lists the fiat and asset pairs, then `quoteRamp(...)` quotes one.\n- The new code finds every route for ARS in AR to USDC, quotes each one for `10_000` ARS (`denomination: 'in'`), and returns the lowest pesos-per-USDC rate. The old code took the first quote's `rate`, which 0.12 no longer returns, so the rate is now computed as `amountIn / amountOut`.\n- Routes or quotes that find no path (`SDK_RAMPS_NO_ROUTE`) are treated as \"no quote\", so the function still returns `null` when nothing quotes. Other errors are rethrown.\n- The `Wallet` screen is unchanged: it still shows `1 USDC = {rate} ARS`.\n\n### `src/balances.ts`: wallet balances\n- `WalletBalanceRecord.balance` is now `string | null`. `null` means the chain could not be read. The old code called `parseFloat` on it, which would throw a type error (and a `NaN` at runtime). A `null` balance now renders as `\"<CODE> unavailable\"`, not as zero, as the SDK asks.\n\n### `src/kyc.ts`: KYC status message\n- `KycStatus` gained `'expired'`. The `switch` now handles it with the line \"Verification expired\". The `switch` had no default, so without this case the typecheck fails.\n\n### `src/App.tsx`, `src/Wallet.tsx`\n- No change. `PollarProvider`, `usePollar`, `login`, `wallet`, `walletBalance`, `refreshWalletBalance` and `getClient` all still exist with the same shapes in 0.12.\n\n## Assumptions to check\n\n- **Ramp units.** The 0.12 typings do not say whether `amountIn` and `amountOut` are human-readable decimals or base units. I assumed decimals, as in the request's `amount.value`. If they are base units, the rate is off by a fixed factor.\n- **Ramp rails.** The app previously let the server choose the payment rail. The new code quotes all AR/ARS/USDC routes, so it is the same request, expressed per rail.\n- **Trustline return value.** `enableUsdc` still returns `true` only for `status === 'success'`. 0.12 can also return `'pending'` (the server-orchestrated path, where the hash is optional). That still returns `false`, as before. I did not change it.\n- **Not tested against the network.** I did not call the Pollar API. The app uses a demo testnet key, and the typecheck is the only check I ran.\n\n## Not done\n\n- No deploy, publish or external submission.\n- `node_modules/` is not in `.gitignore` and appears as untracked. I did not commit it or change `.gitignore`.\n- The 0.12 README points to an `UPGRADE.md` at the repo root that is not in the published package. I used the package's typings and README instead.\n"}}}
